{
  "id": "21686_tabesugiru",
  "headword": "{食|た}べ{過|す}ぎる",
  "reading": "たべすぎる",
  "romaji": "tabesugiru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to overeat; to eat too much",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to overeat; to eat too much",
      "explanation": "Compound of {食|た}べる (to eat) + {過|す}ぎる (to exceed). A very common everyday word."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21686_tabesugiru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{食|た}べ{過|す}ぎてお{腹|なか}が{痛|いた}い。",
      "english": "I ate too much and my stomach hurts.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21686_tabesugiru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{昨日|きのう}の{忘年会|ぼうねんかい}で{食|た}べ{過|す}ぎた。",
      "english": "I overate at yesterday's year-end party.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21686_tabesugiru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{甘|あま}いものを{食|た}べ{過|す}ぎないように{気|き}をつけている。",
      "english": "I'm careful not to eat too many sweets.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "One of the most common ～{過|す}ぎる compounds. Follows the productive V-stem + {過|す}ぎる pattern that means \"to do something too much.\" Conjugates as an ichidan verb.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {食|た}べ{過|す}ぎに{注意|ちゅうい}: watch out for overeating\n- {食|た}べ{過|す}ぎて{気持|きも}ち{悪|わる}い: feel sick from overeating\n- つい{食|た}べ{過|す}ぎてしまう: end up overeating (unintentionally)\n\nRELATED PATTERNS:\n- {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎる: to drink too much\n- {使|つか}い{過|す}ぎる: to use too much\n- {働|はたら}き{過|す}ぎる: to overwork",
